 going to bring his Knight to  d7 many times giving support to his  knight that's usually going to be on f6  here then he can always bring his queen  to c7 very nice place here he has a lot  of sinner control and his dark square  bishop once the e6 has been played can  roam around the board he can Castle  kingside  opening this is going to be very good  for black this is actually one of the  few openings that you'll see where the  mainline black can actually reach  neutrality and in the same time a lot of  people think that black has a better  game especially in the in game where it  comes down to pawn structure life is  actually going to have a better pawn  structure and then white does and we'll  get into that here in a minute play here  continues in the main line with black  moving his knight to g3 obviously we  were attacking it on e4 with our bishop  here and he is now attacking our bishop  so we are going to bring it back to g6  no reason to overextend it yet we don't  have any other pieces out to support  that bishop so we're just going to bring  it back it still has a long diagonal  attacking this c2 square but it's on a  long diagonal right now which is  completely fun and here the main line is  white plays h4 which in the in game is  actually going to hurt his pawn  structure but in the main line it does  start to come down the board and attack  us and get this Bishop which is actually  a very good Bishop for us on the light  square out of the way so we're going to  go ahead and move pawn to h6 in the main  line giving our bishop a layout if he  does continue at the board obviously he  has his knight here on G 3 supporting if  he does push forward that way we can  kick our bishop back to h7 main line  continues with the development of the  night and then we're going to bring our  Knight to d7 we're eventually going to  bring our knight to f6 and this is  merely supporting that and at the same  time it's giving us a little more  central control in a good de